/-!
# KFV §3: the twiddle pass `J_E` (per-record negacyclic rotation by a table)

Records of `r` Gaussian coefficients (`2r` integers) on stack `0`, a table of rotation amounts
`s_j < 2r` (one per record) on stack `14`.

`twC N r = dblI N (2r); rotC N (2r); unpadI N (2r) (4r)`:
double every record to `[z, -z]`, rotate each doubled record (shape `[N, 2r, 2]`) by its table
entry with KFC `rotF` (the table is consumed), keep the first half.

* `twZ r N sv zs`: the result on Gaussian lists; **`twC_spec`** (IL run, cost
  `≤ 10^4 (w+1)(12 N r + 2N + 2) + 70·kap w·4Nr + O(log)`), **`twZ_rep`**: if `zs` represents
  `xs` (`RecRep r F`) then `twZ … zs` represents `twLc r sh Ex xs` when `s_j = sOf r (Ex j)`
  (`J_E` in coefficients, `KFV1Coef`).
